      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Indeed, this needs to be addressed and while a vote kick might work it not only takes time, but gives the bad actor a chance to send out vote kicks of their own to confuse the more unsuspecting guests of the lobby into ignoring all kick requests.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-07-30T18:49:18.337Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, it's possible (and actually happens) for a bad actor to block the owner of an instance, thus letting them disrupt events while making it difficult for the instance owner to notice and kick them. This is a real problem because it's always very apparent who the one person is that has kick powers, and these moderation rights can't be delegated.\nI would suggest the following changes you address this:\n1. It should not be possible to join an instance created by someone you have blocked (or someone who has blocked you). This may mean that blocking someone should also kick them.\n2. Because the above is probably difficult to efficiently implement in a server side manner, the instance owner should be able to see everyone in the instance that they have not blocked themselves, and vice versa.\nWhile this weakens blocking in some ways, it's also critical to ensuring that blocks can't be used to defeat player moderation systems and ruin events.",
